{
  "id": "o9u5ou2",
  "title": "CHAPTER 21: PUBLIC FINANCE",
  "order": 91,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "e6ntpb3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Public Finance encompasses Public Revenue, Public Expenditure, Deficits, Public Debt, and Budgetary Management.",
        "Public Revenue is broadly categorized into Tax Revenue (Direct and Indirect Taxes) and Non-Tax Revenue.",
        "Budgetary Deficits form the core analytical section of public finance, divided into Revenue, Fiscal, and Primary Deficits.",
        "Deficit Financing and Public Debt are crucial mechanisms used by governments to bridge fiscal gaps.",
        "The Finance Commission serves as the key constitutional body managing financial allocations and recommendations."
      ],
      "id": "ri780jj"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Chapter Number",
          "value": "21",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Tax Classification",
          "value": "Direct & Indirect",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Major Deficit Types",
          "value": "3 Key Types",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Body",
          "value": "Finance Commission",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "omey4sp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dpd5wcu",
      "content": "Public Finance is a branch of economics that deals with the income and expenditure of the government."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "myb8691",
      "content": "In simple words, Public Finance explains:"
    },
    {
      "id": "zxv5bsw",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "How the government earns money",
        "How the government spends money",
        "How the government manages deficit and debt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aq9cmbj",
      "content": "Public Finance is very important because modern governments perform many welfare functions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9sc7tem",
      "content": "Without public finance, government cannot run schools, hospitals, defence, roads, railways, etc."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5e793ul",
      "content": "Public Finance is different from Private Finance:"
    },
    {
      "id": "1rqzve4",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Government works for public welfare",
        "Individuals work for personal profit",
        "Government can print money",
        "Individuals cannot print money"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "xk4wpy0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "COMPONENTS OF PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m0uj0zj",
      "content": "Public Finance consists of four main parts:"
    },
    {
      "id": "h8i7f17",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Public Revenue",
        "Public Expenditure",
        "Public Debt",
        "Financial Administration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7bv099y",
      "content": "All these parts work together to manage the economy."
    },
    {
      "id": "bw9rmx7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PUBLIC REVENUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "je8at0a",
      "content": "Public revenue refers to all the income received by the government to meet public expenditure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1erbd3j",
      "content": "The government collects revenue from various sources such as taxes, fees, fines, profits, etc."
    },
    {
      "id": "djjctpv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "TAX REVENUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "34i2jlq",
      "content": "Tax is a compulsory payment made by citizens to the government without any direct return. Types of Taxes:"
    },
    {
      "id": "d35lxop",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Direct Tax",
        "Indirect Tax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bdxl8dc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "DIRECT TAX"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i06frsu",
      "content": "Direct tax is paid directly by the person on whom it is imposed. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "35pokmv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Income Tax</li><li>Corporate Tax</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Income Tax</li><li>Corporate Tax</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Income Tax</li><li>Corporate Tax</li></ul>",
        "Income Tax",
        "Corporate Tax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kwhnqlr",
      "content": "Features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "92kahyy",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Burden cannot be shifted</li><li>Progressive in nature</li><li>Reduces inequality</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Burden cannot be shifted</li><li>Progressive in nature</li><li>Reduces inequality</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Burden cannot be shifted</li><li>Progressive in nature</li><li>Reduces inequality</li></ul>",
        "Burden cannot be shifted",
        "Progressive in nature",
        "Reduces inequality"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "da3bqz3",
      "content": "Merits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "xykbfzq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Promotes equality</li><li>Certain source of income</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Promotes equality</li><li>Certain source of income</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Promotes equality</li><li>Certain source of income</li></ul>",
        "Promotes equality",
        "Certain source of income"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dy9jxnw",
      "content": "Demerits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "4upkx14",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Tax evasion possible</li><li>Discourages savings</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Tax evasion possible</li><li>Discourages savings</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Tax evasion possible</li><li>Discourages savings</li></ul>",
        "Tax evasion possible",
        "Discourages savings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p1s057g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "INDIRECT TAX"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "98m1r34",
      "content": "Indirect tax is paid indirectly by consumers. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "szl537s",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>GST</li><li>Customs Duty</li><li>Excise Duty</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>GST</li><li>Customs Duty</li><li>Excise Duty</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>GST</li><li>Customs Duty</li><li>Excise Duty</li></ul>",
        "GST",
        "Customs Duty",
        "Excise Duty"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mzotaif",
      "content": "Features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "78xi30k",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Burden can be shifted</li><li>Regressive in nature</li><li>Easy to collect</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Burden can be shifted</li><li>Regressive in nature</li><li>Easy to collect</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Burden can be shifted</li><li>Regressive in nature</li><li>Easy to collect</li></ul>",
        "Burden can be shifted",
        "Regressive in nature",
        "Easy to collect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u5zbnxd",
      "content": "GST (Goods and Services Tax):"
    },
    {
      "id": "0cramod",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Introduced in 2017</li><li>One Nation One Tax</li><li>Removed multiple indirect taxes</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Introduced in 2017</li><li>One Nation One Tax</li><li>Removed multiple indirect taxes</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Introduced in 2017</li><li>One Nation One Tax</li><li>Removed multiple indirect taxes</li></ul>",
        "Introduced in 2017",
        "One Nation One Tax",
        "Removed multiple indirect taxes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mwjwyrj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "NON-TAX REVENUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ee9m4c1",
      "content": "Non-tax revenue includes income earned by government other than taxes. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "0p5xc14",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Fees (court fees, school fees)",
        "Fines and penalties",
        "Interest on loans",
        "Profits from public sector enterprises",
        "Grants and donations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c0lil0r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PUBLIC EXPENDITURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4aplt2m",
      "content": "Public expenditure refers to government spending for public welfare and development. Government spends money on:"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b2mld0",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Education",
        "Health",
        "Defence",
        "Infrastructure",
        "Subsidies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sc6ljpf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "TYPES OF PUBLIC EXPENDITURE"
    },
    {
      "id": "606pj4z",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Development Expenditure:<ul><li>Education</li><li>Health</li><li>Agriculture</li><li>Infrastructure</li></ul>",
        "Education",
        "Health",
        "Agriculture",
        "Infrastructure",
        "Non-Development Expenditure:<ul><li>Defence</li><li>Police</li><li>Interest payment</li></ul>",
        "Defence",
        "Police",
        "Interest payment",
        "Capital Expenditure:<ul><li>Construction of roads, dams, railways</li></ul>",
        "Construction of roads, dams, railways",
        "Revenue Expenditure:<ul><li>Salaries</li><li>Pension</li><li>Subsidies</li></ul>",
        "Salaries",
        "Pension",
        "Subsidies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0doi691",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "GOVERNMENT BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5v7ojd6",
      "content": "Government Budget is an annual statement showing expected income and expenditure for a financial year (1st April to 31st March)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9uk2jvc",
      "content": "It reflects government’s economic policies."
    },
    {
      "id": "9wday4u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "TYPES OF BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "id": "mq8m64e",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Balanced Budget:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ranae4n",
      "content": "Income = Expenditure"
    },
    {
      "id": "bc9een7",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Surplus Budget:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "guolzhq",
      "content": "Income &gt; Expenditure"
    },
    {
      "id": "b82i4do",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Deficit Budget:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ricv12t",
      "content": "Expenditure &gt; Income"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Category",
        "Primary Focus / Scope"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Direct Tax",
          "Levied directly on individual income, corporate profits, or wealth where burden cannot be shifted."
        ],
        [
          "Indirect Tax",
          "Levied on goods and services where the burden is shifted to the final consumer."
        ]
      ],
      "id": "idjngv3"
    },
    {
      "id": "9pkqcbr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DEFICITS (MOST IMPORTANT FOR EXAMS)"
    },
    {
      "id": "eap6j0k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "REVENUE DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jqs7woo",
      "content": "Revenue Deficit occurs when:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ssmaa8n",
      "content": "Revenue Expenditure &gt; Revenue Receipts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gqbkvfl",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "33hiwbs",
      "content": "Revenue Deficit = Revenue Expenditure – Revenue Receipts Meaning:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tge557z",
      "content": "Government is not able to meet its regular expenses."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n6cfnwy",
      "content": "Effect:"
    },
    {
      "id": "0p2vyhi",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Bad for economy",
        "Increases debt",
        "Reduces savings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "h8veapp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "FISCAL DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ej0qj7a",
      "content": "Fiscal Deficit shows total borrowing requirement of the government. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nyr11tu",
      "content": "Fiscal Deficit = Total Expenditure – (Revenue Receipts + Non-debt Capital Receipts)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o1awpvz",
      "content": "Meaning:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qqgvm7j",
      "content": "It shows how much money government needs to borrow."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tnqspgb",
      "content": "High Fiscal Deficit leads to:"
    },
    {
      "id": "wquighv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Inflation",
        "Higher interest rates",
        "More public debt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gw2rht8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "PRIMARY DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mo5on1p",
      "content": "Primary Deficit = Fiscal Deficit – Interest Payments"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pogjzvh",
      "content": "It shows the burden of current year's expenses excluding past loans. If Primary Deficit is zero:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8yl35wo",
      "content": "→ Government is managing expenses properly."
    },
    {
      "id": "n7lqnry",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "DEFICIT FINANCING"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0jo1vai",
      "content": "Deficit financing means printing new money or borrowing to meet expenses. Merits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "46bh2kp",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Promotes growth",
        "Helpful in recession"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Differentiating between Revenue Deficit, Fiscal Deficit, and Primary Deficit formulas and concepts.",
        "Classification of Direct vs. Indirect Taxes and Non-Tax Revenue sources.",
        "Role, constitutional mandate, and fiscal distribution functions of the Finance Commission."
      ],
      "id": "prta1ek"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qxpgdhs",
      "content": "Demerits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "uebcvy3",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Causes inflation",
        "Increases debt",
        "Reduces purchasing power"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20fkcxj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PUBLIC DEBT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3yreu45",
      "content": "Public debt refers to loans taken by the government to meet expenditure. Types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "n7qhk8c",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Internal Debt – from RBI, banks, public",
        "External Debt – from IMF, World Bank"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4j8kj1z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "IMPORTANCE OF PUBLIC DEBT"
    },
    {
      "id": "988ke86",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Helps in development",
        "Funds infrastructure",
        "Useful during crisis",
        "Supports economic growth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zhl3t2d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FINANCE COMMISSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "awjekmz",
      "content": "Finance Commission is a constitutional body (Article 280). Functions:"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9pmi2v",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Distribution of taxes between Centre and States",
        "Grants to States",
        "Financial recommendations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "y0km5m0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "IMPORTANCE OF PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "alro7jc",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Promotes economic growth",
        "Reduces inequality",
        "Ensures social welfare",
        "Maintains economic stability",
        "Supports development programs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u4vf2o9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONCLUSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s8hk3gj",
      "content": "Public Finance is the backbone of a modern economy. Efficient management of revenue, expenditure and deficit"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nailfgs",
      "content": "helps in economic development, poverty reduction and welfare of people."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}